From: Logos Maps <maps@logos.co>
Subject: [PATCH] Map: setPlacementTransitionsEnabled

Map::setPlacementTransitionsEnabled(bool) / placementTransitionsEnabled()
expose mbgl::style::TransitionOptions::enablePlacementTransitions, which
the binding's setTransitionOptions(duration, delay) always leaves at the
core default (true).

Why: with placement transitions on, RenderOrchestrator::createRenderTree
marks the symbol placement stale on every frame in which it is not
recomputed (PlacementController::setPlacementStale) and
PlacementController::hasTransitions then reports "needs repaint" for it, so
Map::Impl::onDidFinishRenderingFrame schedules another frame forever
(Continuous mode; the loop recurs after each placement update period). A
Qt Quick item that honours Map::needsRendering therefore repaints
continuously even on an idle map with no symbol layers. Turning the
transitions off (symbols pop instead of fading) lets the map go idle.

The flag lives in the style's transition options and is reset by every
style load; callers re-apply it on MapChangeDidFinishLoadingStyle.

Optional (capability-gated): maps_view idle guarantee (M11.2).

Upstream base: maplibre/maplibre-native-qt c3485f3 (docs/architecture.md section 14.1).
---
 src/core/map.cpp | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/core/map.hpp |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/map.cpp b/src/core/map.cpp
--- a/src/core/map.cpp
+++ b/src/core/map.cpp
@@ -924,6 +924,36 @@
 }
 
 /*!
+    \brief Enable or disable symbol placement transitions.
+    \param enabled Whether placed symbols fade in and out.
+
+    With placement transitions enabled (the core default) the renderer
+    keeps requesting frames while a placement is \e stale, i.e. for as long
+    as the style has a placement at all: RenderOrchestrator marks the
+    placement stale on every frame in which it was not recomputed and
+    reports that as "needs repaint", so a Continuous-mode map never becomes
+    idle. Disabling the transitions makes symbols appear and disappear
+    without fading and lets the map stop rendering when nothing changes.
+
+    The flag is part of the style transition options and is therefore reset
+    whenever a new style is loaded; call this again after
+    \c MapChangeDidFinishLoadingStyle.
+*/
+void Map::setPlacementTransitionsEnabled(bool enabled) {
+    mbgl::style::TransitionOptions options = d_ptr->mapObj->getStyle().getTransitionOptions();
+    options.enablePlacementTransitions = enabled;
+    d_ptr->mapObj->getStyle().setTransitionOptions(options);
+}
+
+/*!
+    \brief Whether symbol placement transitions are enabled.
+    \return \c true if placed symbols fade in and out.
+*/
+bool Map::placementTransitionsEnabled() const {
+    return d_ptr->mapObj->getStyle().getTransitionOptions().enablePlacementTransitions;
+}
+
+/*!
     \brief Add an annotation icon to the map.
     \param name The icon name.
     \param sprite The icon image.
diff --git a/src/core/map.hpp b/src/core/map.hpp
--- a/src/core/map.hpp
+++ b/src/core/map.hpp
@@ -128,6 +128,8 @@
     void setGestureInProgress(bool inProgress);
 
     void setTransitionOptions(qint64 duration, qint64 delay = 0);
+    void setPlacementTransitionsEnabled(bool enabled);
+    [[nodiscard]] bool placementTransitionsEnabled() const;
 
     void addAnnotationIcon(const QString &name, const QImage &sprite);
 
